  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: RNA-only with PCA (config_001) achieves 48.5% accuracy, while image-only with ResNet50 (config_010) achieves only 20.8%, near random. This large gap raises a critical strategic question: is the image modality inherently uninformative for this task, or is ResNet50 simply the wrong architecture for cellular images? 2) What this tests: config_013 uses ImageNet-pretrained ViT-Large (a substantially stronger and more general-purpose vision encoder) with the same singleprofile setting, isolating the effect of image encoder quality. A large improvement over 20.8% would confirm the image modality is viable and that ResNet50 was the bottleneck; a similarly poor result would indicate images are not useful, effectively eliminating ~20 multimodal and image-only configurations from consideration. 3) Why it is the best next experiment: Under a tight budget, resolving whether the image modality is worth pursuing at all has the highest information value—it determines whether the search should focus on RNA improvements (multiprofile, better encoders) or whether multimodal fusion is a realistic path. Without this answer, investing in multimodal configurations (config_016–051) risks wasting experiments on a modality that may contribute no signal. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most consequential design axis (modality viability) before committing budget to more complex combinations."
}

